.TH touch "" "Command"
.SH NAME
touch \- update modification time of a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtouch [\-c] \fIfile ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
touch -- update modification time of a file
Usage:	touch [ -c ] file ...
Option:	-c	Do not create 'file' if it does not exist
.HE
For each named
.IR file ,
.B touch
sets the file's last-modified time to the current time, without
otherwise changing its contents.
By default,
.B touch
creates
.I file
if it does not already exist.
.IP \fB\-c\fR
Do not create
.I file
if it does not exist; instead report the omission and go on to the
next
.IR file .
.PP
.B touch
updates the modification time of an existing, non-empty
.I file
by reading its first byte and writing the same byte back to the same
position; a zero-length
.I file
is instead recreated (unless
.B \-c
is given).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B make
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B touch
reports
.B "touch: cannot create"
followed by the name of
.I file
if
.I file
does not exist and cannot be created, and
.B "touch: write error on"
followed by the name of
.I file
if the rewrite fails; it exits with a nonzero status if this happens
for any
.IR file .
